3. TurboQuant: the TurboQuant KV-cache types (turbo3/turbo4), their CUDA and HIP flash-attention kernels and the
   turboquant rotation data come from the TurboQuant work in the fork by TheTom (branch feature/turboquant-kv-cache).
   Attribution to that work is kept in the commit history of the files it touches.
   That fork is MIT-licensed (GitHub license API for TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant: MIT, checked 2026-10-20).

4. Changes made in this fork (MIT, same as above):
   - an opt-in expert cache in host memory with live resizing, zero slots and a rollback-safe resize
     (src/llama-model.cpp, src/llama-moe-cache-policy.h, tools/server, common/arg.cpp);
   - an opt-in bounded LRU policy for that cache;
   - context (slot) checkpoints for the server's slot save and restore;
   - tests for the cache policy and the argument parser.

5. The HIP and CUDA patch stack that the Shura installer applies on top of this fork (patches/ in the Shura
   repository) is not part of this repository; it is listed and checked by scripts/build-llama.sh there.
